{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1618"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c135): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c135.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1618"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge geography/countries","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/geography__countries.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",941],["+","\n\nNot every large country divides its clocks this way. China is almost as wide as the contiguous United States and spans five geographical time zones, yet since 1949 it has officially used just 1: Beijing Time, UTC+8, from the Pacific coast to the Pamirs. In the far west, in Xinjiang, the sun can rise after 9 a.m. official time, and many Uyghurs keep an unofficial local \"Xinjiang time\" two hours behind Beijing."]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",909],["+","\n\nNicht jedes große Land teilt seine Uhren so auf. China ist fast so breit wie die zusammenhängenden USA und erstreckt sich über fünf geografische Zeitzonen, nutzt aber seit 1949 offiziell nur 1: die Pekinger Zeit, UTC+8, von der Pazifikküste bis zum Pamir. Im fernen Westen, in Xinjiang, kann die Sonne nach 9 Uhr offizieller Zeit aufgehen, und viele Uiguren halten sich an eine inoffizielle „Xinjiang-Zeit“, die zwei Stunden hinter Peking liegt."]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1618"},"reason":"a1618 body: \"China is almost as wide as the contiguous United States\" → \"about as wide\" — China spans ~5,000 km east–west, at least as much as the contiguous US — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_in_China","by":"enrich batch 075","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1018-a1714.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_in_China"}]},
